    "articles": [
      {
        "sequence_id": 1,
        "text": "im ersten Stock means literally 'on the first floor'; in der zweiten Etage means literally 'on the second floor'. In Germany as in many European countries the floors are numbered after the ground floor. The first floor is thus the first floor above the ground and is equivalent to our second floor. The second floor in Germany is equivalent to our third floor, and so on.\n\nhereinkommen is the normal written form. Most speakers in rapid speech elide the first syllable and actually say 'reinkommen, or er kommt 'rein. You will hear the word pronounced both ways."
      }
